From 8219b21126496789321d5f1d47ac5ba3457a92cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:08:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give exported ItemSpaces no collect, as live modelx

Live modelx defines collect only on the declaring Space: reading it on
an ItemSpace raises AttributeError and hasattr is False. The exported
Space class, which its ItemSpace roots share, had collect as a method
that raised TypeError on a root. It is now a property that raises
AttributeError on a root, so exported and compiled models behave as
live; the TypeError check in collect_from_space is gone with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019ikg7LzyawH1Pt5X2iUgyW
---
 doc/source/reference/collect_hook.rst      |  4 ++--
 modelx/export/_mx_sys.py                   |  2 --
 modelx/export/exporter.py                  | 12 ++++++++++--
 modelx/tests/export/test_collect_export.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 4 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/source/reference/collect_hook.rst b/doc/source/reference/collect_hook.rst
index 6e4aeba..886c4fc 100644
--- a/doc/source/reference/collect_hook.rst
+++ b/doc/source/reference/collect_hook.rst
@@ -72,8 +72,8 @@ What modelx guarantees
 * A ``CollectResult`` that the hook returns is stored in the cache and
   returned as it is. :obj:`None` makes modelx evaluate the items itself,
   and that result is stored. Nothing is stored when the hook raises.
-* ``collect()`` called on an ItemSpace raises :obj:`TypeError` before
-  any of this.
+* An ItemSpace has no ``collect``: reading it raises
+  :obj:`AttributeError`, as in live modelx.
 
 When the hook is absent or unknown
 ----------------------------------
